<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_VaporDrifter_AerofleetWiring.xml   UtinniPatches · FORGE_MECHANICS_1 F3
  ============================================================================
  🔴 PLACEHOLDER — proves the wiring PATTERN, per this task's own brief
  ("ship RM_CompVaporDrifter and RM_MapComponent_VaporColumns as generic,
  content-free, compiling classes plus the wiring PATTERN ... a placeholder
  using an EXISTING shipped flying/aerofleet kind ... is fine ... clearly
  commented PLACEHOLDER"). This is NOT a roster decision: whether the
  Forge's actual sky fauna IS AA_Aerofleet (renamed "fumerider" per the kit
  spec's own XML-only ledger line — "Aerofleet→Fumerider rename... roster
  pass") is `rosters/the_forge.json`'s call, owed to that pass, not this one.

  Target: AA_Aerofleet is CONFIRMED already in RUT_TheForge's own
  <wildAnimals> list today (`<AA_Aerofleet MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">
  0.4</AA_Aerofleet>`, RUT_TheForge.xml) — the only sky-capable kind this
  biome already spawns, checked this pass rather than assumed. Its float
  mechanism is confirmed VEF's own class-side CompFloating (see
  RM_CompVaporDrifter.cs's own header) — this patch adds nothing to that,
  it only attaches the pasture-binding data comp alongside it.

  Patched, per this mod's own standing discipline for vendor content: a
  bare PatchOperationAdd rather than a hand-edit of Alpha Animals'
  Races_Aerofleet.xml (a donor mod folder, never touched directly — same
  rule RUT_TibannaTap_BeldonWiring.xml documents for repo-owned-but-generic
  content, applying with even more force to an actual vendor file).

  Gate: PatchOperationFindMod on the kit's display name. ⚠️ MayRequire on
  an <Operation> is INERT — MEASURED 2026-09-17 against 1.6 source:
  ModContentPack.LoadPatches reads every Operation with no attribute check,
  PatchOperation has no such field, and the un-gated comp injection killed
  ALL of Races_Aerofleet.xml on the full-list load (missing type discards
  the whole FILE, then AlphaGenes NREs on the dangling PawnKindDef races).
  FindMod is the only real per-operation gate. If AA_Aerofleet is absent,
  the inner xpath matches nothing and the Add is a silent no-op.

  🔴 What this patch deliberately does NOT do: wire RM_JobGiver_ColumnWander
  into any ThinkTreeDef. forge_kit_spec.md's own F3 resolution defers that
  explicitly ("wired into the sky kind's ThinkTreeDef the same way
  RM_JobGiver_AnchorWander is — a PawnKindDef/ThinkTreeDef content decision,
  XML, owed to the full build — not a further engine question"), and
  MIASMA_MECHANICS_1's own M6 spike left the identical wiring owed for
  RM_JobGiver_AnchorWander. AA_Aerofleet inherits vanilla's shared
  Animal ThinkTreeDef (confirmed this pass — no thinkTree override of its
  own in Races_Aerofleet.xml); splicing a wander-root override into that
  shared tree is authoring judgment (does every Aerofleet everywhere become
  column-bound, or only a Forge-specific rename/clone?) that belongs to the
  roster pass, not this mechanics build. Without that wiring, this comp
  alone grants ground-hazard immunity (RM_GameCondition_WeatherPulse reads
  it directly) but does NOT yet constrain wander — flagged here and in
  FORGE_MECHANICS_1.md, not silently short of the spec's full behaviour.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimMandrake: Environmental Hazards Kit</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Aerofleet"]/comps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.CompProperties_VaporDrifter">
          <forageRadiusBeyondColumns>0</forageRadiusBeyondColumns>
          <groundHazardImmune>true</groundHazardImmune>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
